  "details": "VRChat Version:\n2022.2.1p2:1203 - Oculus\nDescription of the bug:\nIt's going to be somewhat tricky to summarize exactly what's going on, but the basic gist of it is that any movement of my VR controllers or headset, as well as any movement of my avatar I see while holoporting, is only updating at exactly half of whatever my current framerate is! :O\nI can also confirm that this is ONLY a problem in the Oculus build. Switching over to the Steam build, this problem does NOT exist!\nI have an Oculus Rift S, which has an update rate of 80 Hz, so 80 FPS. If things get too intense, I drop to 40 FPS, and if things get REALLY bad because of an unoptimized world or far too many effects, the next step down is 26.667. However, for quite some time now, ALL movement I perform with my headset or controllers is only updating my avatar at half of whatever my current framerate is! So, if my framerate is 80 FPS, my avatar only moves at 40. 40 FPS my avatar only moves at 20. 26.667 FPS my avatar only moves at 13.333.\nHowever, this ONLY affects movement caused either by moving my controllers or headset, as well as any movement I visually watch while holoporting. If I have my avatar play out a canned animation, said animation runs at the full framerate, including anything related to kinematics!\nAlso, this doesn't just affect avatars. Even the LASERS while between worlds are affected!\nAgain, only happening on the Oculus build for Rift / Rift S users. I had a thought to try booting up VRChat in Steam to test this out and this problem is not present in the Steam build!\nSteps to reproduce:\nHappens constantly, from launch to exit, on a PC-based Oculus device. (No idea if Quest devices are affected.)",
